+## HTTP MCP server
+
+Set `App:Mode` to `McpServer` to expose the database-agent contract to an
+external MCP client without initializing or calling the configured LLM:
+
+```json
+{
+  "App": {
+    "Mode": "McpServer"
+  },
+  "Mcp": {
+    "Url": "http://0.0.0.0:5080",
+    "ApiKey": "replace-with-a-long-random-secret"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+The streamable HTTP endpoint is `http://<host>:5080/mcp`. Every request must
+include `Authorization: Bearer <Mcp:ApiKey>`.
+
+For databases with selectable row-security users, call
+`list_security_users`, show the choices to the human, then configure
+`X-Database-User-Id: <selected ID>` as an MCP HTTP header. The header is
+required by SQL tools when users exist and rejected when the database has no
+selectable security users. Identity is never accepted as a tool argument.
+
+| Kind | Name | Purpose |
+|---|---|---|
+| Prompt | `database_agent` | Authoritative workflow, SQL, investigation, and disclosure instructions |
+| Resource | `database://schema` | Complete public table, column, and relationship schema |
+| Tool | `list_security_users` | Valid row-security identities |
+| Tool | `submit_sql` | Deterministically validate, security-filter, and execute final read-only T-SQL |
+| Tool | `investigate_sql` | Execute bounded internal evidence SQL through the same safety boundary |
+
+MCP SQL is never repaired by Ollama or OpenRouter. Parser, schema, read-only,
+metadata-query, investigation-shape, security, and SQL Server errors are
+returned to the external agent. Results are bounded by the existing
+visible-cell settings and include truncation metadata.
+
+`Mcp:ApiKey` must not be empty or `CHANGE_ME`; startup fails otherwise. Prefer
+supplying it through `Mcp__ApiKey`. Binding `0.0.0.0` exposes the service to
+the LAN, so apply firewall controls. Plain HTTP does not encrypt the bearer
+token; use a trusted network or TLS reverse proxy beyond localhost.
+
+A raw protocol example is available at
+`C:\Temp\AiAgentDoc\McpApiIntegration.ps1`.
+
